4.3 Marketing Strategy
Marketing was planned before the birds reached market weight to ensure timely sales and minimize production costs.
The following marketing strategies were adopted:
•	Advance booking of birds by teachers, parents, and members of the local community.
•	Advertising through word of mouth.
•	Display of notices within the school.
•	Promotion during school functions.
•	Direct sales to local consumers.
Potential markets included:
•	School staff.
•	Parents.
•	Local residents.
•	Hotels and restaurants.
•	Local butcheries.
•	Open-air markets within Limuru and surrounding areas.
